"# Master Structure v2.1 — Pass 1, comprehensive\n\n2026-09-26 · @Mohammad AlFalasi\n\n## How to read the master structure\n\nThis is the comprehensive version: every unit of the program, at every depth, with what it teaches, which artifact field it feeds, how it is delivered, and what it needs; the condensed versions are not separate documents but slices of these tables, selected by the Depth column.\n\n**Depth and slices.** O = Orientation, P = Practice, M = Mastery. The Introduction slice is every O unit (about 45 h). The Practitioner slice is every O and P unit with one area (about 200 h). The Comprehensive version is everything (about 480 h with one studio and two tool electives). A single module at any depth is its own product. Change a unit here and every slice changes with it.\n\n",
"**Delivery codes** (a unit usually has two or three): L = lecture material (text, short video; §11 says what qualifies) · C = case, an object or project from the world set told as a story · I = interactive lab (single concept) · S = simulation (compound, several concepts coupled; §9) · P = the AI partner in one of its voices · K = physical making with things at hand · D = a document the learner produces · T = a tool unit is used here.\n\n**Media codes** (§10 has the sourcing): img = images from open collections · drw = drawings, plans, sections · 3d = models · vid = short video · aud = audio · dat = data · ani = animated diagram · pack = a site, object, body or brand pack for a studio brief.\n\n**Artifact field.** The Concept DNA section each unit writes to, by the codes in §2.\n\n**Research status.** Every module is Open: research is uncapped and logged (§12). Status moves to Sprinted (one research sprint done), Drafted (units written), Tested (labs run with people), Live.\n\n",
"**Versioning.** This structure is v2.1. A module's research may add, split, merge, move or re-depth units; each such change increments the structure (v2.2, v2.3…) and is recorded in §12's change log. Nothing here is final by design.\n\n**Regional slot.** Every module's last unit is a regional slot: the same concepts on the learner's own place, and the hook for the Gulf, MENA and SWANA vertical later.\n\n**Counts.** 4 levels, 21 modules, 10 tools modules, 10 compound engines, about 430 units. Numbering is module.unit (F1.3, S2.14) so units can be referenced from anywhere.\n\n## The artifact schema\n\nEvery unit writes to one of these fields; the app holds the artifact as this structure, and the field codes appear in every unit table below.\n\n| Code | Field | Filled mainly by |\n|---|---|---|\n| SRC | Sources, attributions, consultation record | F1, M1, R2 |\n| PRM | Premise: proposition, stance, contradiction, scenario, non-goals | M1 |\n| PER | Perimeter: what the world enables, protects, resists, rejects, transforms | F5, M1 |\n| RUL | Rules: constants, variables, thresholds | M2 |\n| ANT | Anti-DNA | M2 |\n",
"| GRM.f / .m / .k / .c / .s / .a / .sn / .b / .i / .t / .n / .v | Grammars: formal, material, construction (k), chromatic, spatial, atmospheric, sensory, behavioural, interaction, temporal, narrative, verbal | Candidates from F2–F4; rules in M2; refined in areas |\n| ALN | Alignment with practice, collection and masterbrand DNA | M2, R1 |\n| OBL | Category obligations and permitted variation | M2 |\n| TST | Test set: belongs, edge, failure, seductive-but-off | M2, every module's closing test |\n| BRF | Contributor brief and agent prompt architecture | M2, T3 |\n| VER | Version history and change log | M2 onward |\n| COL | Collection map: roles, families, drops, carriers, distribution | M3 |\n| ANC | Anchor expression and family | M4, areas |\n| ADJ | Adjacent translation | M4, areas |\n| JDG | Judged set (briefer lane) | Every module's closing test, briefer lane |\n| CMB | Commissioning brief and record (briefer lane) | Areas, R3 |\n| VEN | Venture: masterbrand, orbital architecture, community, campaign | R1 |\n| RGT | Rights and money: IP protocol, funding scenario, cash model | R2 |\n| HND | Handover package | R3, areas |\n| LCY | Lifecycle: release, maintenance, repair, end of life | R4 |\n",
"| PLW | Planetary weight ledger, accumulating from F5 to R4 | F5, S-areas, T9, R4 |\n| DOS | Dossier: evidence, alternatives, abandoned directions, future practice | R5 |\n| SITE | The site, object, body or brand pack a studio brief runs on | Areas at Mastery |\n\n## Level 0 Orientation and Level 1 Foundations\n\nFoundations is 71 units across five modules; at Practice depth it is a complete global design-literacy course on its own, and its Mastery units are research and specification pieces rather than studios.\n\n### O1 How to see (4 units, all O)\n\n| Unit | Concept | Depth | Field | Delivery | Interactive · media |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| O1.1 | What design does in the world: every made thing tells you what to do, what to feel, who you are | O | — | L, C | img |\n| O1.2 | Read a Room: annotate a space or object for its instructions | O | — | I | Read-a-Room annotator · learner's photo |\n| O1.3 | The artifact you will build, and the two lanes | O | — | L | ani |\n| O1.4 | Meeting the partner: its three voices, what it never does | O | — | P | — |\n\n### F1 Histories of making (35 units, structure v3.6)\n\n| Unit | Concept | Depth | Field | Opening · forms | Voice · media | Was (v2.1) |\n",
