"| F1.21 | Consumer society, the digital and the platform | P | SRC | Story first · 1, 7 | Client · img, vid | F1.15, split |\n| F1.22 | The planetary present: making as extraction | P | SRC, PLW | Data first · 12, 4 | Planet · dat | F1.15, split |\n| F1.22a | Use and consumption: how things were lived with, worn out, repaired, resold, inherited | P | SRC, LCY | Object first · 3, 5 | Mirror · img | new (v3.4) |\n| F1.23 | Obscured labour: the credit map | P | SRC | Object first · 3 | Historian · img | F1.16 |\n| F1.24 | The museum as author: collecting, provenance, restitution | P | SRC | Argument first · 13, 3 | Historian · img | new |\n| F1.25 | Reading an object as history: slow looking and the autopsy in five layers (material, technique, labour, trade, meaning); Practice Reading as its sibling | P | SRC | Lab first · Object Autopsy, full | Mirror · img | F1.17 |\n| F1.26 | Attribution and consultation as protocol, on the CARE principles | P | SRC | Problem first · 2, 15 | Historian · template | F1.18 |\n| F1.27 | Counter-history research piece on one lineage | M | SRC, DOS | Artifact first · Atlas authoring | Historian · learner's material | F1.19 |\n",
"| F1.28 | Primary sources and archives: how to read them | M | SRC | Problem first · Source Grader | Historian · img | F1.20 |\n| F1.28a | Reconstruction: making to know; one technique rebuilt from a primary text, with what the text left unsaid | M | SRC | Making first · operational-sequence strip | Fabricator · primary text, img | new (v3.6) |\n| F1.29 | Vernacular intelligence: oral history, folktale, local taxonomy, with consent | M | SRC | Making first · Oral History Kit | Historian · aud | F1.20a (v3.0 addition) |\n| F1.30 | Re-timing the Atlas: other calendars and periodisations | M | SRC | Data first · Calendars | Historian · dat | new |\n| F1.30a | Counterfactual history: a history of making that did not happen | M | SRC, PRM | Problem first · 1, 13 | Stranger · — | new (v3.4) |\n| F1.31 | Regional slot: the learner's own place, authored locally | M | SRC | Artifact first · Lineage | Historian · learner's material | F1.21 |\n\n",
"**F1 is the first module in the v3 row format.** The Delivery column gives way to the opening move and the presentation forms (numbered as in Final Structure v3.2), the partner voice is named, and Was maps every v2.1 number, so the v3.0 additions F1.3a and F1.20a are now F1.4 and F1.29. Two units at Orientation, twenty-six at Practice, seven at Mastery; about 4 / 22 / 22 hours. Apply by lane, the closing test, the descriptor and the evidence for every change live in the F1 Module File; other modules move to this format when they pass gate G1.\n\n### F2 Form (15 units)\n\n| Unit | Concept | Depth | Field | Delivery | Interactive · media |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| F2.1 | Archetype DNA: what makes a chair a chair | O | GRM.f | I | Typology Dismantler with identity meter · 3d |\n| F2.2 | Figure and ground; positive form and negative interval | O | GRM.f | I | Figure-Ground lab · img |\n| F2.3 | Visual weight and tension | O | GRM.f | I | Visual Gravity game |\n| F2.4 | Typology theory: archetypes, types, models | P | GRM.f | L, C | img |\n| F2.5 | Proportion and modular systems: classical, Renaissance, modular | P | GRM.f | C, I | Grid Lab · drw |\n",
