"Every tool concept in the original can grow along one path — a single lab, then a coupled lab that takes another unit's output as its input, then a layer in one of the compound engines of §9 — and the tables below give each tool its units and that path; T1–T5 are the core thread at Practice, T6–T10 are Mastery electives, and every tool has a free route.\n\n**Evolution study** (the same tool, three sizes)\n\n| Tool concept | First used in | Single lab | Coupled lab | Engine layer | Free route |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| T1 Seeing and drawing | F2, S1.7 | Orthographic Trainer: draw the plan of a rotating object with overlay feedback | Draw the section of your own Adjacency Builder plan; the trainer checks it against the model | World Engine and Object Line accept the learner's drawings as inputs, and the Handover Auditor reads them | pencil, paper, phone camera; in-app canvas |\n",
"| T2 Parametric thinking | F2.13, M3 | One rule, many outputs in p5.js | The Typology Dismantler's sliders are exposed as a node graph the learner rewires | Family Generator drives the Collection Matrix: change a rule, the whole family and its costs update | p5.js in the browser; Blender geometry nodes; Grasshopper only if licensed |\n| T3 Working with AI | M2.15 | Prompt Architecture Studio with drift score | Agent Team Builder briefs three roles from the DNA and compares their outputs | Stranger Lab across media (text, image, 3D sketch); the partner's voices are built on this | free model tiers or program-provided access, logged |\n| T4 Simulation | F3.8, S1.31 | A scene, a light, a walk (three.js template) | The Sequence Choreographer's path becomes the walk; the Light Sandbox's lights are the scene's lights | World Engine, Site Work and Product Loop are real-time engines with layers switched on per unit | three.js templates; Godot for heavier work |\n",
"| T5 Honest evidence | M4, S1.31 | Render Honesty Audit: what does this picture claim about scale, material, cost | PBR Material Lab fed by the Material Card Deck's chosen materials | Every engine's export runs through the audit before it enters the dossier | Blender |\n| T6 Reality capture | S1.5, S2.19 | Phone photogrammetry of an object with a quality checker | The capture becomes the buck in the Object Line, or the existing building in the Palimpsest Tool | World Engine on a captured site | free photogrammetry apps and open point-cloud viewers |\n| T7 Data visualisation | M1, F5 | Encoding Chooser on a supplied dataset | Synthesis Board data becomes a node map; Route Map takes the learner's data | Translation Engine (S4) spatialises data into the Site Work engine | d3 in-app; open datasets |\n| T8 Physical computing | S2.30, S3.25 | Sensor-to-actuator logic in a browser simulator | State-Indicator Designer runs on the simulated board | Object Line's cyber-physical layer | free microcontroller simulators; hardware optional |\n",
"| T9 Environmental analytics | F5.6, S1.19 | Climate Simulation Lite for a latitude | Planetary Ledger takes the BOM from Object Line or the materials from the Material Dossier | World Engine's climate layer; Capsule's heat-stress layer; the final ledger | open climate tools; openLCA |\n| T10 Fabrication | S1.17, S2.20 | Toolpath Previewer on a supplied part | Print Failure Predictor on the learner's own Family Generator output | Object Line's making layer: route, tolerance, failure, cost together | free CAM previewers; slicer software |\n\n### T1 Seeing and drawing (5 units)\n\n| Unit | Concept | Depth | Delivery | Interactive · media |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| T1.1 | Observational and analytical drawing: gesture, line weight, mass, silhouette | P | K, I | Line-Weight Coach · learner's photos |\n| T1.2 | Orthographic logic: plan, section, elevation, exploded axonometric | P | I | Orthographic Trainer · 3d |\n| T1.3 | Movement notation and state changes | P | I | Movement Notation Sketcher · vid |\n| T1.4 | Ideation sketching and the physical buck | P | K | paper, card |\n| T1.5 | Full orthographic and exploded set of a real assembly | M | K, D | Orthographic Trainer, authoring · drw |\n\n",
